1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,510
Sodium acetate.

2
00:00:01,510 --> 00:00:04,023
The sodium ion is a spectator.

3
00:00:04,023 --> 00:00:15,208
But acetate is the conjugate base of a weak acid, so it pulls a proton off a water molecule, forming acetic acid and leaving a hydroxide ion behind.

4
00:00:15,208 --> 00:00:17,513
The solution turns alkaline.

5
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:19,791
This is anionic hydrolysis.

